  "slug": "dark-energy-543b",
  "summary": "Eight November 2026 preprints test dynamical dark energy against DESI, CMB and supernova data, with independent SN Ia datasets aimed at the w0-wa tension.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is testing departures from a cosmological constant using DESI BAO or full-shape data with CMB, supernovae and lensing. Model-level work compares one-parameter vacuum histories within VCDM, where F42 is favored by AIC with supernovae, and a full-shape DESI DR1 analysis finds the scalar-field Fading Dark Sector model outperforming CPL w0-wa. Two non-parametric reconstructions of dark-energy density and gravitational response report a phantom-divide crossing near z≈0.5–0.7, one also asking whether dark energy clusters. A generalised axion-like quintessence model is confronted with multiple probes. Complementary efforts target systematics: the LEMAITRE project and a ZTF/SNLS/HSC calibration proposal provide independent SN Ia constraints, while a 0i Einstein-equation proposal offers observable-only tests of dark-sector degeneracies.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
